WHY / design decisions for this increment (Paper Comprehension Tutor backend):

Scope choice: the spec replaces Space Invaders wholesale, but doing the removal
+ frontend in the same commit would leave a broken half-state if interrupted.
The Ralph loop favors small green increments, so this commit lands ONLY the
backend foundation + service layer (additive), leaving the game's `/` route and
frontend intact and all suites green. Game removal happens in the integration
increment once paper views/islands exist.

Key technical decisions:
- EmbeddingVector(TypeDecorator): single model definition that resolves to
  pgvector Vector on PostgreSQL and JSON-text on SQLite. This honors the spec's
  "keep pgvector isolated; don't let SQLite-incompatible columns break the
  SQLite test suite" caveat WITHOUT a second model definition (single source of
  truth, no adapters).
- Models subclass Base (not db.Model): mypy strict's disallow_subclassing_any
  rejects subclassing db.Model (typed Any). The pre-existing hello model used
  the same Base pattern. db = SQLAlchemy(model_class=Base) so Base IS db.Model
  for metadata registration.
- FakeAiClient as the single hermetic seam: tests assert OUR behaviour (prompt
  assembly, JSON parsing, score clamping, citation sanitization, persistence)
  rather than mocking the OpenAI SDK everywhere. Same fake powers USE_FAKE_AI=1
  for the future E2E run (no token/network). Deterministic hash-based embeddings
  mean identical text -> cosine similarity 1.0, which the retrieval test relies on.
- GitHubModelsClient._client typed as Any: the OpenAI SDK's overloaded create()
  produced a call-overload error in envs WITH the SDK and an unused-ignore error
  in the pre-commit mypy env WITHOUT it. Typing the client Any makes the call
  untyped in both, eliminating the environment-dependent typing split.
- embeddings.search dialect branch: pgvector cosine (<=>) on PostgreSQL, NumPy
  in-Python ranking elsewhere, identical (chunk, score) return shape. The
  PostgreSQL branch wraps in try/except -> Python fallback so a pgvector hiccup
  degrades gracefully instead of 500ing.
- tutor citation sanitization: model-returned cited_chunk_ids are filtered to the
  set actually retrieved this turn; empty/invalid -> fall back to retrieved ids,
  guaranteeing every grounded reply carries real provenance. Score clamped 0-100
  in the Pydantic validator so an out-of-range model value can never persist.
- session middleware resets the per-request "set cookie" flag in before_request
  because Flask `g` is app-context scoped; the test client shares one app context
  across requests, which previously leaked the flag and re-set the cookie.

Not yet done (next increments): controllers, paper/chat views + blueprint swap,
templates, frontend islands (upload/analysis/chat) + react-markdown, game
removal, E2E spec, and applying the migration against a real PostgreSQL (no local
psql/Postgres in this environment).
